18"}], "value": "Catalyzes the condensation of (S)-aspartate-beta-semialdehyde [(S)-ASA] and pyruvate to 4-hydroxy-tetrahydrodipicolinate (HTPA)"}], "commentType": "FUNCTION"}, {"commentType": "CATALYTIC ACTIVITY", "reaction": {"name": "L-aspartate 4-semialdehyde + pyruvate = (2S,4S)-4-hydroxy-2,3,4,5-tetrahydrodipicolinate + H2O + H(+)", "reactionCrossReferences": [{"database": "Rhea", "id": "RHEA:34171"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:15361"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:15377"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:15378"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:67139"}, {"database": "ChEBI", "id": "CHEBI:537519"}], "ecNumber": "4.3.3.7", "evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000256", "source": "ARBA", "id": "ARBA00047836"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000256", "source": "HAMAP-Rule", "id": "MF_00418"}]}}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000256", "source": "ARBA", "id": "ARBA00005120"}, {"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000256", "source": "HAMAP-Rule", "id": "MF_00418"}], "value": "Amino-acid biosynthesis; L-lysine biosynthesis via DAP pathway; (S)-tetrahydrodipicolinate from L-aspartate: step 3/4"}], "commentType": "PATHWAY"}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000256", "source": "HAMAP-Rule", "id": "MF_00418"}], "value": "Homotetramer; dimer of dimers"}], "commentType": "SUBUNIT"}, {"commentType": "SUBCELLULAR LOCATION", "subcellularLocations": [{"location": {"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000256", "source": "HAMAP-Rule", "id": "MF_00418"}], "value": "Cytoplasm", "id": "SL-0086"}}]}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000256", "source": "HAMAP-Rule", "id": "MF_00418"}], "value": "Belongs to the DapA family"}], "commentType": "SIMILARITY"}, {"texts": [{"evidences": [{"evidenceCode": "ECO:0000256", "source": "HAMAP-Rule", "id": "MF_00418"}], "value": "Was originally thought to be a dihydrodipicolinate synthase (DHDPS), catalyzing the condensation of (S)-aspartate-beta-semialdehyde [(S)-ASA] and pyruvate to dihydrodipicolina